BAMBI IS ALIVE AND WELL

26
00:01:36,023 --> 00:01:37,525
KINES INGREDIENT ANALYSIS

27
00:01:40,653 --> 00:01:43,531
[Louis] Myosin, actin, myogen,

28
00:01:43,614 --> 00:01:46,826
then tongkat, and phosphate of maca?

29
00:01:47,368 --> 00:01:48,244
Is that it?

30
00:01:48,828 --> 00:01:51,288
{\an8}<i>It is. At least for the meat
and bone part.</i>

31
00:01:51,372 --> 00:01:53,916
{\an8}This stuff is
in a commercially available drink?

32
00:01:54,542 --> 00:01:56,961
{\an8}No wonder it causes meat intoxication.

33
00:01:57,044 --> 00:01:58,212
{\an8}<i>But that's the thing.</i>

34
00:01:58,295 --> 00:02:00,798
{\an8}<i>There's not enough in it
to set its drinkers off like that.</i>

35
00:02:00,881 --> 00:02:01,715
{\an8}Seriously?

36
00:02:02,299 --> 00:02:04,593
Then, could it be something else?

37
00:02:04,677 --> 00:02:05,928
[Chloe] <i>I think so.</i>

38
00:02:06,011 --> 00:02:08,764
<i>My theory is that it's somehow
reacting with another substance</i>

39
00:02:08,848 --> 00:02:10,808
<i>to light up the central nervous system.</i>

40
00:02:11,642 --> 00:02:13,686
So it needs some kind of catalyst.

41
00:02:13,769 --> 00:02:15,354
{\an8}[Chloe] <i>Hmm.</i>

42
00:02:15,437 --> 00:02:19,191
{\an8}<i>Considering that herbivores don't seem
to show any symptoms when they drink it,</i>

43
00:02:19,275 --> 00:02:21,402
{\an8}<i>it must be something unique to carnivores.</i>

44
00:02:22,027 --> 00:02:23,404
{\an8}Then what is it?

45
00:02:23,487 --> 00:02:25,447
{\an8}<i>That's outside my area of expertise.</i>

46
00:02:26,073 --> 00:02:28,993
{\an8}<i>Still, I know a researcher
who could probably help you out.</i>

47
00:02:29,076 --> 00:02:31,287
Do they work at your lab too?

48
00:02:31,370 --> 00:02:33,956
<i>Mmm-mmm. He, uh, works somewhere else.</i>

49
00:02:34,456 --> 00:02:35,958
<i>And he's sort of...</i>

50
00:02:36,041 --> 00:02:37,877
Uh, what is it?

51
00:02:38,377 --> 00:02:41,338
<i>He's very talented, but he is a bit shady.</i>

52
00:02:41,422 --> 00:02:43,007
Would you mind introducing me--

53
00:02:43,090 --> 00:02:45,634
- [crackles]
- [yelps, groans]

54
00:02:45,718 --> 00:02:47,219
<i>Hey. What happened?</i>

55
00:02:47,303 --> 00:02:51,015
<i>Are you okay? Answer me, please.
Do you hear me?</i>

56
00:02:51,599 --> 00:02:52,433
{\an8}<i>Louis!</i>

57
00:02:54,351 --> 00:02:56,061
{\an8}[strains] I'm all right.

58
00:02:56,645 --> 00:02:58,689
Could you send me his contact details?

59
00:02:58,772 --> 00:02:59,940
[ends call]

60
00:03:00,024 --> 00:03:02,484
[groaning]

61
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:05,362
<i>What's going on?</i>

62
00:03:07,031 --> 00:03:09,950
<i>I know I fed everything
from the knee down to Legoshi.</i>

63
00:03:12,119 --> 00:03:14,705
<i>Could something have happened
to him? Legoshi?</i>

64
00:03:16,123 --> 00:03:17,833
CALL ENDED

65
00:03:17,917 --> 00:03:19,251
{\an8}KOPI LUWAK RESEARCH CENTER
DESHICO

66
00:03:19,335 --> 00:03:20,502
HAPPY & HEAVEN
JUNGLE THEATER

67
00:03:20,586 --> 00:03:22,171
[Luna] We said we don't know.

68
00:03:22,254 --> 00:03:25,507
You really have no idea
who that big bad wolf was?

69
00:03:25,591 --> 00:03:29,511
How many times do I have to tell you?
The owner set us up and we did our thing.

70
00:03:29,595 --> 00:03:30,596
[Miguel] Come on.

71
00:03:30,679 --> 00:03:33,641
Do you think we're the type of idiots
who'd nod their heads and walk away

72
00:03:33,724 --> 00:03:35,517
after a half-assed story like that?

73
00:03:35,601 --> 00:03:38,312
You're the type of idiots to keep us here
after we told the truth.

74
00:03:38,395 --> 00:03:39,230
Screw this.

75
00:03:39,313 --> 00:03:41,857
Given your line of work,
we'd hate to do anything

76
00:03:41,941 --> 00:03:44,944
that might leave a mark
on those spectacular bodies of yours.

77
00:03:45,027 --> 00:03:47,446
So just tell us. It'll make this easier.

78
00:03:47,529 --> 00:03:49,657
We don't know shit!

79
00:03:50,574 --> 00:03:53,452
[Free clicks tongue] That's a damn shame.

80
00:03:54,328 --> 00:03:55,788
Have it your way, then.

81
00:03:57,498 --> 00:03:58,791
[Cosmo gasps]

82
00:03:58,874 --> 00:04:01,961
Sorry about this,
but we can't go home empty-handed.

83
00:04:04,129 --> 00:04:05,881
By the time we all got here,

84
00:04:05,965 --> 00:04:08,717
you two had already
made yourselves scarce.

85
00:04:08,801 --> 00:04:10,135
- [Luna] Huh?
- Got that?

86
00:04:10,928 --> 00:04:13,681
I made a promise to a former boss of ours.

87
00:04:13,764 --> 00:04:16,433
I told him that I'd keep you both safe.

88
00:04:16,517 --> 00:04:19,603
[Cosmo] Was your former boss
that little fawn boy?

89
00:04:19,687 --> 00:04:22,231
The Shishi-Gumi always keeps its promises.

90
00:04:24,566 --> 00:04:25,442
[both exhale]

91
00:04:26,235 --> 00:04:28,570
[Free] We'll find our souvenirs
somewhere else.

92
00:04:31,407 --> 00:04:34,201
Hey, we had orders to kill those two.

93
00:04:34,285 --> 00:04:36,954
- You sure about this?
- [Free grunts]

94
00:04:37,037 --> 00:04:38,497
Yep, it's all good.

95
00:04:39,081 --> 00:04:39,915
[Free] Hmm?

96
00:04:42,251 --> 00:04:43,877
- [Free grunts]
- [Agata] Huh?

97
00:04:44,461 --> 00:04:46,505
[Free panting]

98
00:04:48,048 --> 00:04:50,551
[panting]

99
00:04:54,013 --> 00:04:55,139
[Louis] <i>Damn it, Zoozle.</i>

100
00:04:55,222 --> 00:04:57,182
<i>At least factor in places
like the Black Market</i>

101
00:04:57,266 --> 00:04:59,310
<i>when you calculate your routes.</i> [groans]

102
00:04:59,852 --> 00:05:01,854
<i>If they catch me here, I'm done for.</i>

103
00:05:02,813 --> 00:05:03,939
[pants]

104
00:05:09,695 --> 00:05:11,280
{\an8}[Free] Hmm. [gasps softly]

105
00:05:15,909 --> 00:05:17,661
- [crackles]
- [grunts, sighs]

106
00:05:18,829 --> 00:05:19,663
[beeps]

107
00:05:20,706 --> 00:05:22,541
[Louis] <i>This needs some maintenance.</i>

108
00:05:23,334 --> 00:05:24,168
[gasps]

109
00:05:28,505 --> 00:05:29,548
[Free growls softly]

110
00:05:32,259 --> 00:05:33,135
Boss?

111
00:05:33,218 --> 00:05:34,053
[huffs]

112
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:35,804
[Free] Hmm.

113
00:05:36,513 --> 00:05:40,225
I can't imagine you've forgotten
our very last agreement.

114
00:05:41,518 --> 00:05:44,605
Promised you that if I ever saw you
in the Black Market again,

115
00:05:44,688 --> 00:05:46,231
I'd kill you on the spot.

116
00:05:47,483 --> 00:05:51,070
Yeah. I guess I failed to hold up
my end of the bargain.

117
00:05:52,196 --> 00:05:53,030
Do it.

118
00:05:55,074 --> 00:05:57,910
[Free] <i>Damn it. Why does it have to be me?</i>

119
00:05:58,827 --> 00:06:00,079
[Louis] <i>Don't hesitate.</i>

120
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:03,540
[Free] <i>First Ibuki, now him.</i>

121
00:06:03,624 --> 00:06:06,251
<i>Why am I always the one
who has to pull the trigger?</i>

122
00:06:07,795 --> 00:06:09,379
[Louis] <i>What's with that look?</i>

123
00:06:09,463 --> 00:06:12,382
[scoffs] <i>Aren't you the king of beasts?</i>

124
00:06:12,466 --> 00:06:14,760
[Free] <i>Not even a hint of fear
on your face.</i>

125
00:06:15,844 --> 00:06:20,224
<i>I knew all along
you really were the best boss we ever had.</i>

126
00:06:20,307 --> 00:06:21,141
[gunshot]

127
00:06:32,402 --> 00:06:33,529
[Free exhales shakily]

128
00:06:34,154 --> 00:06:35,447
[antler clatters]

129
00:06:35,531 --> 00:06:37,366
[Louis] <i>I shed my antlers.</i>

130
00:06:38,575 --> 00:06:40,160
<i>Is it that time already?</i>

131
00:06:41,995 --> 00:06:44,706
Sorry to throw off your aim there.
Go ahead.

132
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:48,293
[Free chuckles]

133
00:06:48,377 --> 00:06:52,089
I said I'd kill you
if I saw you again, correct?

134
00:06:52,172 --> 00:06:54,007
That was the promise, wasn't it?

135
00:06:55,008 --> 00:06:59,138
But from where I'm standing, you don't
look like anybody I've ever seen before.

136
00:06:59,221 --> 00:07:01,431
[laughing]

137
00:07:03,267 --> 00:07:05,185
- I've missed you so much!
- Hey!

138
00:07:06,353 --> 00:07:08,230
- Free really might kill him.
- [Louis] Enough!

139
00:07:09,106 --> 00:07:11,150
- Stop it already!
- [all laughing]

140
00:07:14,778 --> 00:07:17,531
- [Jimma] Oh. Those are sick!
- Hey! [exclaims playfully]

141
00:07:17,614 --> 00:07:20,534
[Agata] Look at you without your antlers.
You're like a fawn.

142
00:07:20,617 --> 00:07:21,785
Can it.

143
00:07:21,869 --> 00:07:25,414
Man, what a waste.
They grew so beautifully.

144
00:07:25,497 --> 00:07:27,374
So, what will you do with these?

145
00:07:27,458 --> 00:07:29,460
If you want to keep them,
they're all yours.

146
00:07:29,543 --> 00:07:32,963
- Whoo! [laughs, exclaims]
- Yes! Ex-boss is the best!

147
00:07:33,046 --> 00:07:35,257
By the way,
as long as we're patching you up,

148
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:36,300
how's your leg?

149
00:07:36,383 --> 00:07:37,968
Noticed you were walking funny.

150
00:07:38,635 --> 00:07:40,596
Oh, yeah. I lost my right leg.

151
00:07:40,679 --> 00:07:42,181
- [all] What?
- Huh?

152
00:07:44,141 --> 00:07:45,809
- It's so shiny!
- [all exclaiming]

153
00:07:45,893 --> 00:07:48,479
[Louis sighs] I'm used to losing
body parts,

154
00:07:48,562 --> 00:07:50,355
what with shedding antlers and all.

155
00:07:50,439 --> 00:07:51,607
It's not a big deal.

156
00:07:52,691 --> 00:07:53,692
More importantly,

157
00:07:54,985 --> 00:07:57,946
I want to know
why you guys look so emaciated.

158
00:07:58,572 --> 00:07:59,615
[sighs]

159
00:08:00,324 --> 00:08:04,203
Thing is, we're explicitly limited
to eating meat two times a month.

160
00:08:04,286 --> 00:08:07,039
Just another exciting
new Shishi-Gumi rule.

161
00:08:07,706 --> 00:08:10,709
And if you sneak some
behind that asshole's back, he'll know,

162
00:08:10,792 --> 00:08:12,503
and then... [clicks tongue]

163
00:08:13,086 --> 00:08:14,046
"That asshole"?

164
00:08:14,129 --> 00:08:16,840
Anyway, what brought you
to the Black Market?

165
00:08:16,924 --> 00:08:17,799
Oh...

166
00:08:18,550 --> 00:08:21,428
Uh, the Kopi... Hang on.

167
00:08:23,514 --> 00:08:24,765
[all] "Kopi Luwak"?

168
00:08:25,724 --> 00:08:27,100
[all exhale]

169
00:08:27,184 --> 00:08:28,435
Do you know the place?

170
00:08:28,519 --> 00:08:30,145
[Jimma] Uh, yeah.

171
00:08:30,229 --> 00:08:32,606
[whistling in distance]

172
00:08:33,190 --> 00:08:35,275
- It's the boss!
- [Victor] He's here early.

173
00:08:42,533 --> 00:08:43,408
Huh?

174
00:08:43,492 --> 00:08:46,036
It stinks, but it should cover your scent
while we hide you.

175
00:08:46,119 --> 00:08:48,830
[whistling grows louder]

176
00:08:56,505 --> 00:08:57,422
[whistling stops]

177
00:08:59,007 --> 00:09:02,135
Guess what! I brought you kittens
a little souvenir today.

178
00:09:04,763 --> 00:09:06,139
[lions gasp]

179
00:09:06,223 --> 00:09:09,851
[Melon] Yeah, he may have been
an absolute failure as a guard, but...

180
00:09:09,935 --> 00:09:13,146
[inhales sharply] I think he should
make for a decent decoration.

181
00:09:13,730 --> 00:09:15,816
- [all gasp]
- [Melon] All right, then.

182
00:09:15,899 --> 00:09:18,694
Let's have ourselves
a round of stripper steaks.

183
00:09:19,653 --> 00:09:21,029
[Louis] <i>A gazelle?</i>

184
00:09:21,113 --> 00:09:22,739
<i>No, those fangs...</i>

185
00:09:23,574 --> 00:09:24,408
<i>A mix?</i>

186
00:09:27,578 --> 00:09:29,830
[Melon] Huh? What the hell is this?

187
00:09:30,872 --> 00:09:33,917
We arrived too late.
The strippers got away.

188
00:09:34,001 --> 00:09:37,462
So, in turn, we took what was owed
from the club's owner instead.

189
00:09:37,546 --> 00:09:39,089
Huh.

190
00:09:39,172 --> 00:09:42,676
And you actually thought this would make
for an acceptable replacement

191
00:09:42,759 --> 00:09:44,177
for the dinner I asked for?

192
00:09:44,261 --> 00:09:46,471
[Agata] We're getting paid
pretty well there.

193
00:09:46,555 --> 00:09:47,556
[Melon] Hmm?

194
00:09:47,639 --> 00:09:49,224
But even if we weren't,

195
00:09:49,308 --> 00:09:52,603
we're not so desperate for food
that we'd eat someone on our turf.

196
00:09:53,562 --> 00:09:54,896
Well, well.

197
00:09:55,564 --> 00:09:58,233
I must admit I'm impressed.

198
00:09:58,317 --> 00:10:00,319
[inhales sharply]
You really put a lot of thought

199
00:10:00,402 --> 00:10:03,614
into how your actions
might play out here, didn't you?

200
00:10:03,697 --> 00:10:06,033
- [splutters nervously] Uh, yeah.
- [chuckles]

201
00:10:06,116 --> 00:10:08,285
- [Melon grunts]
- [Agata screaming]

202
00:10:11,788 --> 00:10:15,500
Agata, the Congo lion, 26 years old.

203
00:10:16,084 --> 00:10:19,004
You truly are the baby of the Shishi-Gumi.

204
00:10:19,087 --> 00:10:20,756
[screaming]

205
00:10:20,839 --> 00:10:23,216
Ah, a dull little boy

206
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:26,094
who clings to his imagined
sense of lionly pride

207
00:10:26,178 --> 00:10:29,056
because it allows him to pose
as being an adult.

208
00:10:29,681 --> 00:10:30,766
Anyway. Free.

209
00:10:30,849 --> 00:10:32,017
Uh-- Yes?

210
00:10:32,893 --> 00:10:35,395
There's an outsider
in this room, isn't there?

211
00:10:36,438 --> 00:10:37,272
Hmm?

212
00:10:38,106 --> 00:10:41,610
Tell me, how stupid
do you idiots think I am?

213
00:10:42,653 --> 00:10:45,947
I could smell them as soon
as I walked in, you lying little shits.

214
00:10:48,450 --> 00:10:51,161
- Come on. What are you sitting around for?
- [groaning]

215
00:10:51,244 --> 00:10:53,789
Bring out our little visitor
so I can get a good look at him.

216
00:10:54,539 --> 00:10:56,958
Our guest or Agata.

217
00:10:57,042 --> 00:10:59,336
Time for you to choose
who I'll be serving for dinner.

218
00:11:00,379 --> 00:11:01,672
I can't hear you!

219
00:11:02,881 --> 00:11:06,259
- [Louis] <i>I have to show myself.</i>
- [Miguel] I'm sorry, boss.

220
00:11:06,343 --> 00:11:07,177
Huh?

221
00:11:19,398 --> 00:11:21,108
Ah. Ha!

222
00:11:21,191 --> 00:11:23,652
I thought that I smelled deer.
What do you know?

223
00:11:23,735 --> 00:11:26,863
Those antlers are so fresh
that the blood on them is still wet.

224
00:11:26,947 --> 00:11:28,240
Care to explain?

225
00:11:28,949 --> 00:11:31,451
I disobeyed your orders, boss.

226
00:11:31,535 --> 00:11:33,495
Couldn't keep my cravings in check.

227
00:11:33,578 --> 00:11:36,415
I found a deer on the Black Market,
and I ate it.

228
00:11:37,499 --> 00:11:38,792
I won't make excuses.

229
00:11:39,501 --> 00:11:41,545
Because there is no excuse.

230
00:11:41,628 --> 00:11:43,213
Carnivores like us,

231
00:11:43,296 --> 00:11:45,549
we're foolish creatures
led only by instinct.

232
00:11:46,591 --> 00:11:47,759
That's all we are.

233
00:11:48,343 --> 00:11:50,762
As a singular mix
of carnivore and herbivore,

234
00:11:51,304 --> 00:11:53,265
you could be called a perfect creature,

235
00:11:54,141 --> 00:11:56,059
and I am but a mere lion.

236
00:11:57,310 --> 00:12:00,939
I couldn't even follow a simple rule
like only eating meat twice a month.

237
00:12:01,022 --> 00:12:02,482
[Louis sighs]

238
00:12:02,566 --> 00:12:05,068
But I promise,
if you give me another chance,

239
00:12:05,152 --> 00:12:06,027
{\an8}- I swear...
- [gasps]

240
00:12:06,611 --> 00:12:08,947
{\an8}[Miguel] I swear that
I'll never eat meat again

241
00:12:09,030 --> 00:12:12,492
so that I can work on becoming
even slightly as perfect as you.

242
00:12:13,243 --> 00:12:15,036
[groans]

243
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:18,165
For a foolish creature,
you're using your head rather well.

244
00:12:18,874 --> 00:12:20,667
[breath trembles]

245
00:12:21,251 --> 00:12:24,546
I was hoping to enjoy
a nice, relaxing dinner, but...

246
00:12:24,629 --> 00:12:28,091
[inhales sharply] now that Yahya's aware
of my connection with you kittens,

247
00:12:28,175 --> 00:12:31,052
I probably shouldn't hang around
this place for too long.

248
00:12:34,806 --> 00:12:35,682
Huh?

249
00:12:35,765 --> 00:12:37,309
KOPI LUWAK RESEARCH CENTER

250
00:12:37,392 --> 00:12:40,937
[chuckles nervously] I've got holes
in my pockets lately, I guess.

251
00:12:41,021 --> 00:12:41,897
Is that so?

252
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:45,817
Anyone ever tell you that your handwriting
is weak and skinny like an herbivore's?

253
00:12:46,651 --> 00:12:48,653
[Melon whistling]

254
00:12:53,366 --> 00:12:55,952
[Agata grunts, yells]

255
00:12:56,745 --> 00:12:58,955
Who'd have thought
you were such a performer?

256
00:12:59,039 --> 00:13:01,166
Never knew you had that groveling in you.

257
00:13:01,249 --> 00:13:03,335
[Miguel chuckles] It was nothing.

258
00:13:04,044 --> 00:13:06,296
- [rattling]
- [all] Huh?

259
00:13:07,839 --> 00:13:09,216
I don't know what to say.

260
00:13:10,342 --> 00:13:12,135
Anything but freaking thanks.

261
00:13:12,219 --> 00:13:15,055
We wouldn't be lions
if we didn't look out for our pride.

262
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:19,643
So, your next stop is Kopi Luwak?

263
00:13:19,726 --> 00:13:20,560
Yeah.

264
00:13:21,311 --> 00:13:23,063
I've been looking into Kines.

265
00:13:24,064 --> 00:13:25,565
[all sighing]

266
00:13:27,025 --> 00:13:29,945
CENTRAL HOSPITAL
LARGE ANIMAL WARD

267
00:13:30,529 --> 00:13:32,864
- [machine beeping]
- [groans]

268
00:13:37,452 --> 00:13:38,286
Huh?

269
00:13:39,454 --> 00:13:40,413
Huh?

270
00:13:41,498 --> 00:13:42,374
Huh.

271
00:13:43,083 --> 00:13:43,917
Mmm.

272
00:13:53,593 --> 00:13:56,221
[gasps] <i>That's right! Melon shot me.</i>

273
00:13:57,514 --> 00:13:59,349
<i>And I guess someone brought me here.</i>

274
00:14:00,183 --> 00:14:01,184
[gasps]

275
00:14:02,561 --> 00:14:04,604
<i>Tha-- That's me!</i>

276
00:14:06,439 --> 00:14:07,399
Huh?

277
00:14:09,317 --> 00:14:10,318
[shudders]

278
00:14:14,239 --> 00:14:15,490
[shudders]

279
00:14:16,825 --> 00:14:17,742
[exhales]

280
00:14:21,162 --> 00:14:25,625
<i>So, does this mean
I'm stuck between life and death?</i>

281
00:14:27,002 --> 00:14:29,546
<i>Am I... Am I going to die?</i>

282
00:14:31,172 --> 00:14:34,885
[sighs frustratingly] If I knew this was
going to happen, I would've...

283
00:14:35,427 --> 00:14:38,263
I would've given Haru that kiss
when I still had the chance.

284
00:14:38,346 --> 00:14:40,640
Ah, sorry, Haru.

285
00:14:41,683 --> 00:14:44,144
I wonder if she'll cry
when she hears that I died.

286
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:47,522
Nah, she'll probably just be mad.

287
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:50,150
[sighs heavily]

288
00:14:50,984 --> 00:14:53,862
[female] Isn't it a little soon
to be giving up like that?

289
00:14:53,945 --> 00:14:56,948
Well, I don't know. Just look at me.

290
00:14:57,908 --> 00:14:58,742
Huh?

291
00:14:59,993 --> 00:15:00,827
Huh?

292
00:15:02,871 --> 00:15:03,872
Huh?

293
00:15:07,542 --> 00:15:08,376
Mom?

294
00:15:11,421 --> 00:15:12,756
<i>I can't believe it.</i>

295
00:15:13,506 --> 00:15:17,135
<i>My mom died six years ago,
but she's standing right in front of me.</i>

296
00:15:17,844 --> 00:15:20,597
Look at how big you've gotten, Legoshi.

297
00:15:22,515 --> 00:15:23,725
[Legoshi] <i>Wait, is this...</i>

298
00:15:27,479 --> 00:15:28,772
You silly boy.

299
00:15:28,855 --> 00:15:30,774
You know,
you always used to be so reserved.

300
00:15:30,857 --> 00:15:32,817
Now you leap into danger whenever you can.

301
00:15:32,901 --> 00:15:33,735
Well, I...

302
00:15:33,818 --> 00:15:36,154
You really do know
how to make a mother worry.

303
00:15:36,237 --> 00:15:37,238
I'm sorry.

304
00:15:38,031 --> 00:15:39,699
But I just couldn't stand there

305
00:15:39,783 --> 00:15:43,161
and let Melon keep calling himself
a freak, a thing, an abomination

306
00:15:43,244 --> 00:15:45,580
because I know that you're mixed too,

307
00:15:45,664 --> 00:15:49,042
and, you know, if Haru and I decide
to have a kid someday,

308
00:15:49,125 --> 00:15:51,044
obviously, they'd be mixed.

309
00:15:51,628 --> 00:15:53,004
It kind of made me wonder

310
00:15:53,088 --> 00:15:57,008
if our kid would see themself
as some kind of abomination.

311
00:15:57,592 --> 00:16:00,345
Well, that is what they'd be.

312
00:16:01,513 --> 00:16:02,806
What?

313
00:16:06,685 --> 00:16:07,852
[footsteps approaching]

314
00:16:07,936 --> 00:16:08,770
[Yahya sighs]

315
00:16:09,562 --> 00:16:12,774
[Yahya] It's been five days.
You need something in your stomach.

316
00:16:15,986 --> 00:16:16,820
[sighs]

317
00:16:18,530 --> 00:16:20,824
[Leanno] <i>Your grandfather
was a Komodo dragon,</i>

318
00:16:21,408 --> 00:16:23,368
and your grandmother was a gray wolf.

319
00:16:24,202 --> 00:16:26,204
And together, they gave birth to me.

320
00:16:27,205 --> 00:16:30,583
<i>Given their rather unique pairing,
people were naturally curious.</i>

321
00:16:31,710 --> 00:16:34,879
<i>They wanted to see what sort
of ugly creature the two created.</i>

322
00:16:34,963 --> 00:16:36,256
[Legoshi] Hmm.

323
00:16:36,339 --> 00:16:38,550
Of course, much to their chagrin,

324
00:16:38,633 --> 00:16:41,636
I grew up to be a beautiful wolf,
and a fine model at that.

325
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:46,016
{\an8}[Legoshi] Oh, hey, I remember these.
Grandpa must've put them in the scrapbook.

326
00:16:46,099 --> 00:16:48,643
{\an8}[Leanno] I'll have you know
that back in my day,

327
00:16:48,727 --> 00:16:52,022
{\an8}"Leanno the Gray Wolf" was quite
the sensation in the modeling world.

328
00:16:52,105 --> 00:16:54,315
[Legoshi] Hmm. Yeah, I can see it.

329
00:16:54,399 --> 00:16:57,235
You wouldn't believe
how in I was. [chuckles]

330
00:16:57,318 --> 00:16:59,195
- That's why...
- Huh?

331
00:16:59,279 --> 00:17:01,448
[melancholy music playing]

332
00:17:01,531 --> 00:17:04,659
I don't want anyone to know
my dad's a Komodo dragon.

333
00:17:04,743 --> 00:17:07,328
We're going to have to keep you
a secret. I'm sorry.

334
00:17:09,456 --> 00:17:11,124
Don't worry about it, sweetheart.

335
00:17:11,708 --> 00:17:15,628
At least you and I can share a nice meal
without my venom causing any problems.

336
00:17:15,712 --> 00:17:19,799
And us eating together,
well, that alone makes me happy.

337
00:17:20,884 --> 00:17:21,968
Just live your life.

338
00:17:24,054 --> 00:17:25,805
[Leanno] <i>I was truly loved.</i>

339
00:17:28,308 --> 00:17:30,185
<i>Even then, I was afraid.</i>

340
00:17:31,186 --> 00:17:32,979
<i>No matter what I did or said,</i>

341
00:17:33,688 --> 00:17:36,483
<i>Komodo dragon blood
still flowed through my veins.</i>

342
00:17:37,275 --> 00:17:39,110
[humming]

343
00:17:39,194 --> 00:17:42,030
[chuckling]

344
00:17:43,281 --> 00:17:44,699
Looking good. [gasps]

345
00:17:47,118 --> 00:17:49,829
[screams]

346
00:17:52,582 --> 00:17:55,919
<i>The doctor told me it was
some rare genetic something or other</i>

347
00:17:56,002 --> 00:17:57,420
<i>that manifested with age</i>

348
00:17:58,004 --> 00:18:00,465
<i>and that there was nothing
that could be done.</i>

349
00:18:02,759 --> 00:18:05,553
- [female 1] Ew, do you see that?
- [female 2] Disgusting.

350
00:18:05,637 --> 00:18:08,181
- [gasps]
- [female 3] Don't come near me.

351
00:18:08,264 --> 00:18:10,600
- [whimpering]
- [female 3] How filthy.

352
00:18:10,683 --> 00:18:12,811
- She's venomous. Don't touch her.
- [whimpering]

353
00:18:12,894 --> 00:18:15,188
[male 1] Put her down
if she's that dangerous.

354
00:18:15,730 --> 00:18:18,149
- [male 2] Stay back.
- [male 3] Just die already.

355
00:18:19,359 --> 00:18:21,444
[Leanno whimpering]

356
00:18:23,530 --> 00:18:25,532
[Leanno] <i>I was neither wolf nor lizard.</i>

357
00:18:26,449 --> 00:18:29,452
<i>No. I had no place in this world.</i>

358
00:18:30,203 --> 00:18:32,247
<i>Just a strange creature without a name.</i>

359
00:18:34,791 --> 00:18:36,042
<i>An abomination.</i>

360
00:18:38,419 --> 00:18:39,379
<i>And so...</i>

361
00:18:41,131 --> 00:18:43,133
[melancholy music continues playing]

362
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:46,845
[females whispering indistinctly]

363
00:19:08,741 --> 00:19:10,827
[Leanno] <i>The night before I killed myself,</i>

364
00:19:11,327 --> 00:19:14,122
<i>I came to snuggle with you
for a little while.</i>

365
00:19:16,124 --> 00:19:19,502
<i>I'm so sorry that I didn't say anything.</i>

366
00:19:20,420 --> 00:19:24,048
<i>I suppose I was a selfish mother,
right up until the very end.</i>

367
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:27,468
[Legoshi] <i>I should have said something.</i>

368
00:19:28,136 --> 00:19:30,180
<i>- I'm sorry.</i>
- [Leanno] <i>What?</i>

369
00:19:30,263 --> 00:19:31,181
[Legoshi] <i>I was...</i>

370
00:19:32,098 --> 00:19:33,474
<i>I was awake that night.</i>

371
00:19:34,392 --> 00:19:39,772
<i>I thought your scales and your fur,
both looked so beautiful.</i>

372
00:19:39,856 --> 00:19:42,025
[Leanno gasps] <i>You did?</i>

373
00:19:42,901 --> 00:19:46,988
[Legoshi] <i>I wanted to press my cheek
to yours, to turn around and hug you.</i>

374
00:19:48,281 --> 00:19:49,574
<i>For you to hug me.</i>

375
00:19:50,867 --> 00:19:52,285
<i>Because in all the world,</i>

376
00:19:53,328 --> 00:19:54,996
<i>you're the only mom I've got.</i>

377
00:19:55,580 --> 00:19:58,458
[Leanno cries] <i>That makes me so happy.</i>

378
00:19:58,541 --> 00:20:00,460
[sniffles] <i>Thank you.</i>

379
00:20:03,129 --> 00:20:06,090
That night, I thought
if I didn't say anything,

380
00:20:06,174 --> 00:20:07,800
if I didn't look at you,

381
00:20:07,884 --> 00:20:10,136
it would make things
easier on you somehow.

382
00:20:11,095 --> 00:20:13,139
I had no idea
that's what you were thinking about.

383
00:20:13,223 --> 00:20:14,057
[Legoshi] Mmm.

384
00:20:16,017 --> 00:20:18,770
[sighs deeply] Why didn't I just
turn around that night?

385
00:20:20,021 --> 00:20:23,733
Oh, Mom, I wish I could have told you
what I thought.

386
00:20:24,776 --> 00:20:26,110
Thank you for that.

387
00:20:27,070 --> 00:20:28,071
And you're right.

388
00:20:28,905 --> 00:20:31,241
There's a chance that
if I'd heard those words,

389
00:20:31,324 --> 00:20:33,034
things could've gone differently.

390
00:20:34,327 --> 00:20:37,789
But I'm afraid I can't undo what I did.

391
00:20:38,373 --> 00:20:40,541
And that's why it's so important

392
00:20:40,625 --> 00:20:43,711
that you reach out to all the mixed beasts
who are suffering in the world.

393
00:20:44,337 --> 00:20:45,838
And do it in your own words.

394
00:20:46,756 --> 00:20:48,216
In my own words?

395
00:20:48,841 --> 00:20:51,511
Yes, in your unique way.

396
00:20:51,594 --> 00:20:53,888
Think of all of the different scars
on your body.

397
00:20:54,514 --> 00:20:58,017
Each and every one of them
is just like another one of your words.

398
00:21:00,186 --> 00:21:01,396
Oh.

399
00:21:03,648 --> 00:21:06,150
I know what I want to do. It's clear now.

400
00:21:07,568 --> 00:21:09,070
Then you better not forget it.

401
00:21:10,446 --> 00:21:13,199
You've inherited blood
from both me and your grandpa.

402
00:21:13,283 --> 00:21:16,035
You're kinder and stronger
than anybody else.

403
00:21:17,620 --> 00:21:18,538
You think so?

404
00:21:20,581 --> 00:21:23,584
Legoshi, I'll always love you.

405
00:21:29,299 --> 00:21:30,258
Hmm?

406
00:21:30,341 --> 00:21:31,175
[music ends]

407
00:21:32,510 --> 00:21:33,386
[both gasp]

408
00:21:34,554 --> 00:21:35,722
[Gosha] Legoshi?

409
00:21:38,099 --> 00:21:39,100
[Gosha] Hmm.

410
00:21:49,235 --> 00:21:51,237
[howling]

411
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,123
[closing theme song playing]

412
00:22:02,206 --> 00:22:04,792
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

413
00:22:04,876 --> 00:22:08,254
<i>♪ Keep it beating on and on ♪</i>

414
00:22:09,422 --> 00:22:12,592
<i>♪ I don't want to live without it ♪</i>

415
00:22:13,384 --> 00:22:15,720
<i>♪ You give me the strength inside ♪</i>

416
00:22:17,764 --> 00:22:20,975
<i>♪ Some things aren't meant to be ♪</i>

417
00:22:21,059 --> 00:22:23,603
<i>♪ You say it like you know ♪</i>

418
00:22:23,686 --> 00:22:26,189
<i>♪ But I really want you ♪</i>

419
00:22:27,648 --> 00:22:31,527
<i>♪ I want you to see it the way I do ♪</i>

420
00:22:32,570 --> 00:22:36,783
<i>♪ 'Cause every time I think about you ♪</i>

421
00:22:37,408 --> 00:22:40,036
<i>♪ My heartbeat goes a-risin' ♪</i>

422
00:22:40,119 --> 00:22:44,832
- <i>♪ And I just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

423
00:22:44,916 --> 00:22:46,793
- <i>♪ Till I... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

424
00:22:46,876 --> 00:22:48,002
<i>♪ Till I die ♪</i>

425
00:22:48,086 --> 00:22:52,507
<i>♪ There's nothing
That can beat like this ♪</i>

426
00:22:53,216 --> 00:22:56,511
<i>♪ Faster as I close my eyes ♪</i>

427
00:22:56,594 --> 00:23:00,765
- <i>♪ Just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

428
00:23:00,848 --> 00:23:02,767
- <i>♪ Till the... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

429
00:23:02,850 --> 00:23:04,102
<i>♪ Till the night ♪</i>

430
00:23:04,852 --> 00:23:09,148
<i>♪ Now as long as you are here by my side ♪</i>

431
00:23:09,232 --> 00:23:10,566
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

432
00:23:10,650 --> 00:23:12,652
<i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>

433
00:23:13,402 --> 00:23:16,364
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

434
00:23:17,406 --> 00:23:19,325
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

435
00:23:19,408 --> 00:23:24,455
{\an8}- <i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

436
00:23:25,414 --> 00:23:28,918
{\an8}- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>
- <i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>
